1
00:07:13,333 --> 00:07:19,333
The Dead Don't Hurt is a western, drama film directed by Viggo Mortensen.

2
00:14:26,666 --> 00:14:32,666
In the 1860s, fiercely independent French-Canadian Vivienne Le Coudy embarks on a journey with Danish
immigrant Holger Olsen, attempting to forge a life together in the dusty town of Elk Flats, Nevada.

3
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:46,000
When Holger decides to go fight for the Union in the burgeoning Civil War, Vivienne must
fend for herself, which isn't easy in a town controlled by a corrupt mayor.

4
00:28:53,333 --> 00:28:59,333
Vivienne Le Coudy, played by Vicky Krieps.

5
00:36:06,666 --> 00:36:12,666
Holger Olsen, played by Viggo Mortensen.

6
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:26,000
Weston Jeffries, played by Solly McLeod.

7
00:50:33,333 --> 00:50:39,333
Alfred Jeffries, played by Garret Dillahunt.

8
00:57:46,666 --> 00:57:52,666
Rudolph Schiller, played by Danny Huston.

9
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
Alan Kendall, played by W. Earl Brown.

10
01:12:13,333 --> 01:12:19,333
The Dead Don't Hurt
(French: Jusqu’au bout du monde,
Spanish: Hasta el fin del mundo,
Danish: Til Verdens Ende)
is a 2023 Western film written, directed, and produced by
Viggo Mortensen, and starring Mortensen, Vicky Krieps, Solly McLeod, Garret Dillahunt, Colin Morgan, Ray McKinnon, Luke Reilly, Atlas Green, and Danny Huston.

11
01:19:26,666 --> 01:19:32,666
Mortensen also composed the score to the film.

12
01:26:40,000 --> 01:26:46,000
It is a co-production among Canada, Denmark and Mexico.

13
01:33:53,333 --> 01:33:59,333
The Dead Don't Hurt premiered at the Toronto
International Film Festival on September 8, 2023.

14
01:41:06,666 --> 01:41:12,666
It had a theatrical release in North America on May 31, 2024,
and was released in Denmark on June 13, 2024.

15
01:48:20,000 --> 01:48:26,000
The film received generally favourable reviews from critics.

16
01:55:33,333 --> 01:55:39,333
The film explores themes of immigration, leaving one's family,
sexual violence, american civil war, 1860s.

17
02:02:46,666 --> 02:02:52,666
The tone is emotional.
